  ('zcrm_1579374000001982215', NULL, 'Future Prospect', 'zcrm_1579374000000088015', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Other', 'Tricia', 'Carson-Pellis', 'zcrm_1579374000000157741', 'Wendy Scipione', 'TCar312@gmail.com', NULL, '720-341-4500', NULL, NULL, '1969-12-18', 'zcrm_1579374000000088015', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2016-03-03 16:56:21', '2025-08-08 14:51:49', 'Tricia Carson-Pellis', NULL, 'Commerce City, Adams County', 'CO', '80022', FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'USD', 1.0, '2025-08-08 14:51:49', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Daughter- Claims her on taxes', 'Apr-96', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '3-4-16 Tricia is approved for Medicaid bc. unemployment benes only run for 26 months now and can''t necessarily renew. So, income will $14,066 moving forward. Was earning $4583 a month before company just shut down 3-4-16. She''s happy to be on Medicaid while not earning anything. Just applied for her, not for her daughter because she''s covered under her x-husband''s plan.

Super complicated situation. Husband will cover both of her daughters but she claims one daughter born 4/16/96 on her taxes. She only wants coverage for herself. Was hoping to qualify for Medicaid but income is too high still. Her boyfriend Adam needs coverage for him and 2 or 3 if his kids. He makes about $55K MAGI. He needs his own plan. He and his kids have been on Tricia''s plan in the past as a domestic partner. But, I don''t think that''s possible when getting a subsidy since they file their taxes separately. He''s a tobacco user and likely not wanting to quit. Next step is to apply for Medicaid for both of them separately tomorrow.', 'Kaiser', 'Is fine with Kaiser bc used to work for them.', '0', '0.0', 'Health Insurance', NULL, '2016-04-01', 'Steve Hakes', NULL, NULL, 'false', 'false', '0', '0', NULL, '0', NULL, 'Female', NULL, NULL, NULL, '0', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Converted', NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'Contacts_2026_03_20.csv'),
