  ('zcrm_1579374000001607101', NULL, 'Future Prospect', 'zcrm_1579374000000088015', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Non-Member Referral', 'Steve', 'Spencer', 'zcrm_1579374000000157741', 'Wendy Scipione', 'steve.spencer.art@gmail.com', NULL, '720-560-0178 day', NULL, '303-443-0121 eve', '1952-04-29', 'zcrm_1579374000000088015', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2016-01-22 13:59:22', '2025-08-08 14:51:47', 'Steve Spencer', NULL, 'Boulder', 'CO', '80302', FALSE, NULL, 'deefish7@gmail.com', 'USD', 1.0, '2025-08-08 14:51:47', NULL, 'Denise / Dee', '4/10/1954', 'Youngest Son- Turning 26 in Aug. 2016', NULL, 'Eldest Son Dustin- 35', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2-18-16 Spoke with Dee extensively. She''s going to apply for HES and understands she will have to pay for any skin issues in the first year if they already were being watched. But, regular insurance will cost $650-$1154 a month and still cover little to nothing. Only carriers that accept Dee''s two doctors are Anthem and Humana. She also takes sertraline 100 mg 2x daily which will cost under $9 mo. with GoodRX and Lorazepam 1 mg 60 tablets also less than $9 mo. Will cost her less than she''s paying with insurance now which is $15 mo. Dee can also pay out of pocket for her OT which will still be better than trying to charge through regular insurance.  They have 2 sons who may also benefit from HES. Dustin is 25 in CO living at home. Noah is 36 and living in NY. Neither are covered now.

1-22-16 Works for Celestial Seasonings and is turning 64 years old in two months. Wife may be ok on HES. Will decide after speaks with Dermatologist and her OT. Sons might be good candidates for HES. "I have history of skin cancer, and although I haven''t needed surgeries for a few years, I do go often, every three months, and get the spray that freezes off skin issues, or potential pre-cancerous sites. Sometimes I need to have biopsies as well." Also sees Dr. Fran Hamilton and Dr. Fran Hamilton.

Steve had heart condition/stints put into his heart 4 years ago. Has regular check ups and thinks it''s best to stick with regular ins. for this last year until he turns 65. Looked at silver or gold Anthem plans for him.', 'Anthem', 'Maybe Anthem for Steve and HES for Denise (If her OT isn''t too costly and if not at huge risk of skin cancer in first year).', '0', '0.0', 'To Be Determined', NULL, '2016-05-01', 'Susan Davis', NULL, NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Male', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Converted', NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'Contacts_2026_03_20.csv'),
