  ('zcrm_1579374000000234399', 'Jeff Kanter', 'In-Active', 'zcrm_1579374000000237303', 'Advanced Consulting', 'Denny''s he is one of employees fiance''s', 'Adam', 'McElvy', 'zcrm_1579374000000237065', 'Jeff Kanter', 'amcelvy@noemail.com', NULL, '540-293-1222', NULL, NULL, '1983-06-04', 'zcrm_1579374000000084003', 'Rod Maxson', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2015-08-16 13:19:19', '2025-08-08 14:51:41', 'Adam McElvy', '928 Morgan Ave SE', 'Roanoke City', 'VA', '24013', FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'USD', 1.0, '2025-08-08 14:51:41', NULL, NULL, '0000-00-00', NULL, '0000-00-00', NULL, '0000-00-00', NULL, '0000-00-00', '225-31-079', '<b>12/03/2014 04:43 PM</b>: <b>3/19/2014 08:20 PM</b>: JeffK spoke enrolled in health and dental<hr><b>3/19/2014 07:15 PM</b>: Bronze Deductible Only POS Plan POS Point of Service: A type of plan in which you pay less if you use doctors, hospitals, and other health care providers that belong to the plan%u2019s network. POS plans also require you to get a referral from your primary care doctor in order to see a specialist. | Bronze Plans are put into 5 categories. These 5 categories (catastrophic, bronze, silver, gold, and platinum) are based on how you and the plan expect to share the costs for health care. Bronze plans cover 60% of the total average cost of care. The category you choose affects how much your premium costs each month and what portion of the bill you pay for things like hospital visits or prescription drugs. It also affects your total out-of-pocket costs - the total amount you''ll spend for the year if you need lots of care. Coventry Health Care of Virginia, Inc. APPLYDETAILS Monthly premium   $0/mo One enrollee Premium before tax credit $205/mo Deductible The amount you owe for health care services your health insurance or plan covers before your health insurance or plan begins to pay. For example, if your deductible is $1,000, your plan won''t pay anything until you%u2019ve met your $1,000 deductible for covered health care services subject to the deductible. The deductible may not apply to all services. $6,300/yr  Per individual  Out-of-pocket Maximum Your expenses for medical care that aren''t reimbursed by insurance. Out-of-pocket costs include deductibles, coinsurance, and copayments for covered services plus all costs for services that aren''t covered. $6,300/yr  Per individual  Copayments/Coinsurance: A copay is a fixed amount (for example, $15) you pay for a covered health care service, usually when you get the service. The amount can vary by the type of covered health care service. Coinsurance is your share of the costs of a covered health care service, calculated as a percent (for example, 20%) of the allowed amount for the service. You pay coinsurance plus any deductibles you owe. For example, if the health insurance or plan%u2019s allowed amount for an office visit is $100 and you''ve met your deductible, your coinsurance payment of 20% would be $20. The health insurance or plan pays the rest of the allowed amount. Primary Doctor: No Charge after Deductible Specialist Doctor: No Charge after Deductible Generic Prescription: No Charge after Deductible ER Visit: No Charge after Deductible<hr><b>3/19/2014 07:14 PM</b>: JeffK VM-LM  30 , living in Roanoke City County, VA.   Based on a household size of one and income of $16,000, you may qualify for a $209/month tax credit<hr><hr />', 'To Be Determined', 'Coventry Bronze Deductible Only POS Plan', '205', '7.0', 'To Be Determined', NULL, '2014-05-01', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Import', NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL,