  ('zcrm_1579374000000234439', 'Jeff Kanter', 'In-Active', 'zcrm_1579374000000237303', 'Advanced Consulting', 'Razvan Chircu', 'Gelu Marius', 'Marcu', 'zcrm_1579374000000237065', 'Jeff Kanter', 'marius73marcu@yahoo.com', NULL, '954-275-4854', NULL, '954-275-4854', '1973-03-29', 'zcrm_1579374000000084003', 'Rod Maxson', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2015-08-16 13:19:19', '2025-08-08 14:51:41', 'Gelu Marius Marcu', '4174 Inverrary Dr', 'Lauderdale', 'FL', '33319', FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'USD', 1.0, '2025-08-08 14:51:41', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '592-75-243', '<b>3/03/2015 12:54 PM</b>: <b>12/10/2014 08:39 AM</b>: JeffK spoke and enrolled over the phone at healthgov. $225 subsidy<hr><b>12/03/2014 04:43 PM</b>: <b>3/29/2014 07:31 PM</b>: JeffK enrolled on line healthgov<hr><b>3/29/2014 04:23 PM</b>: JeffK set up accouint he is waiting on health gov email will call me<hr><b>3/29/2014 04:12 PM</b>: Silver $10 Copay HMO Carelink HMO Health Maintenance Organization: A type of health insurance plan that usually limits coverage to care from doctors who work for or contract with the HMO. It generally won''t cover out-of-network care except in an emergency. An HMO may require you to live or work in its service area to be eligible for coverage. HMOs often provide integrated care and focus on prevention and wellness. | Silver Plans are put into 5 categories. These 5 categories (catastrophic, bronze, silver, gold, and platinum) are based on how you and the plan expect to share the costs for health care. Silver plans cover 70% of the total average cost of care. The category you choose affects how much your premium costs each month and what portion of the bill you pay for things like hospital visits or prescription drugs. It also affects your total out-of-pocket costs - the total amount you''ll spend for the year if you need lots of care. CoventryOne APPLYDETAILS Monthly premium   $0/mo One enrollee Premium before tax credit $216/mo Deductible The amount you owe for health care services your health insurance or plan covers before your health insurance or plan begins to pay. For example, if your deductible is $1,000, your plan won''t pay anything until you%u2019ve met your $1,000 deductible for covered health care services subject to the deductible. The deductible may not apply to all services. $0/yr  Per individual  Out-of-pocket Maximum Your expenses for medical care that aren''t reimbursed by insurance. Out-of-pocket costs include deductibles, coinsurance, and copayments for covered services plus all costs for services that aren''t covered. $1,500/yr  Per individual  Copayments/Coinsurance: A copay is a fixed amount (for example, $15) you pay for a covered health care service, usually when you get the service. The amount can vary by the type of covered health care service. Coinsurance is your share of the costs of a covered health care service, calculated as a percent (for example, 20%) of the allowed amount for the service. You pay coinsurance plus any deductibles you owe. For example, if the health insurance or plan%u2019s allowed amount for an office visit is $100 and you''ve met your deductible, your coinsurance payment of 20% would be $20. The health insurance or plan pays the rest of the allowed amount. Primary Doctor: No Charge Specialist Doctor: $25 Generic Prescription: $5 ER Visit: $100<hr><b>3/29/2014 04:11 PM</b>: JeffK spoke  41 , living in Broward County, FL.   Based on a household size of one and income of $13,000, you may qualify for a $225/month tax credit<hr><hr><hr />', 'To Be Determined', 'Coventry $10 Co-pay Silver', '246.38', '6.0', 'To Be Determined', NULL, '2015-01-01', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL